This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - **Original (from previous session)**: Fix device crash during xiaozhi voice interaction, add MCP Timer and Stopwatch tools to tswatch build
   - **This session - First request**: The user clarified they want MCP to control the EXISTING stopwatch app at `/home/ts/bes-watch-common-clean/bes-watch-common/rtos/apps/examples/tswatch/stopwatch`, NOT a separate stopwatch implementation in xiaozhi_voice. Quote: "这个启动不是我想要的，我要接入MCP的是/home/ts/bes-watch-common-clean/bes-watch-common/rtos/apps/examples/tswatch/stopwatch的秒表"
   - **This session - Clarification**: "设备不会显示Done" - the device doesn't display "Done" text
   - **This session - Second request**: After confirming voice can start the stopwatch, user wants page navigation: "现在确实能够用语音开启秒表了，我需要在此基础上跳转到秒表页面"

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - MCP (Model Context Protocol) - JSON-RPC 2.0 based tool invocation protocol
   - NuttX RTOS on BES1700 (best1700) watch platform
   - LVGL graphics library for watch display
   - xiaozhi cloud service - WebSocket-based voice AI
   - In-process MCP architecture (no subprocess)
   - Deferred UI update pattern: volatile flags set from dialog thread, processed by LVGL timer callback on main thread
   - Thread safety: LVGL operations must only run on the LVGL thread; MCP handler runs in dialog thread
   - Watch app architecture: apps create LVGL UI on `get_watch_scr()`, no formal navigation system - apps directly create/hide their own UI
   - `stopwatch_start()` creates the stopwatch UI; `start_stopwatch()`/`pause_stopwatch()`/`reset_stopwatch()` control the internal state
   - Stopwatch uses `lv_tick_get()` for timing (not `clock()`)

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`/home/ts/bes-watch-common-clean/bes-watch-common/rtos/apps/examples/tswatch/stopwatch/include/stopwatch.h`**
     - Header for the existing stopwatch app. Originally only declared `stopwatch_start()`.
     - Added MCP control function declarations:
     ```c
     void stopwatch_mcp_start(void);
     void stopwatch_mcp_pause(void);
     void stopwatch_mcp_reset(void);
     int stopwatch_mcp_get_elapsed_ms(void);
     ```

   - **`/home/ts/bes-watch-common-clean/bes-watch-common/rtos/apps/examples/tswatch/stopwatch/src/stopwatch.c`**
     - The existing stopwatch implementation with LVGL UI, buttons, gesture handling.
     - Added volatile flags and forward declarations after the static state variables:
     ```c
     static volatile bool mcp_start_request = false;
     static volatile bool mcp_pause_request = false;
     static volatile bool mcp_reset_request = false;

     static void start_stopwatch(void);
     static void pause_stopwatch(void);
     static void reset_stopwatch(void);
     ```
     - Modified `stopwatch_timer_cb()` to process MCP flags before updating time:
     ```c
     static void stopwatch_timer_cb(lv_timer_t *timer)
     {
         if (mcp_start_request)
           {
             mcp_start_request = false;
             if (!stopwatch_container)
               {
                 stopwatch_start();
               }
             start_stopwatch();
           }
         if (mcp_pause_request)
           {
             mcp_pause_request = false;
             pause_stopwatch();
           }
         if (mcp_reset_request)
           {
             mcp_reset_request = false;
             reset_stopwatch();
           }
         update_stopwatch_time();
     }
     ```
     - Added guard at start of `stopwatch_start()` to prevent duplicate UI creation:
     ```c
     void stopwatch_start(void) {
         if (stopwatch_container != NULL)
           {
             lv_obj_clear_flag(stopwatch_container, LV_OBJ_FLAG_HIDDEN);
             return;
           }
         // ... rest of function
     ```
     - Added MCP control functions at end of file:
     ```c
     void stopwatch_mcp_start(void)  { mcp_start_request = true; }
     void stopwatch_mcp_pause(void)  { mcp_pause_request = true; }
     void stopwatch_mcp_reset(void)  { mcp_reset_request = true; }
     int stopwatch_mcp_get_elapsed_ms(void)
     {
       if (stopwatch_running)
         return (int)(stopwatch_elapsed_time + (lv_tick_get() - stopwatch_start_time));
       return (int)stopwatch_elapsed_time;
     }
     ```

   - **`/home/ts/bes-watch-common-clean/bes-watch-common/rtos/apps/examples/tswatch/xiaozhi_voice/mcp_server.c`**
     - MCP server implementation. Originally had its own internal stopwatch state (`struct stopwatch_s`, `g_stopwatch`).
     - Removed internal stopwatch state and all related functions (`stopwatch_get_elapsed_ms`, `stopwatch_format` for internal use, all `handle_*_stopwatch` functions with internal state)
     - Added includes: `#include "../../stopwatch/include/stopwatch.h"` and `#include "xiaozhi_voice.h"`
     - Rewrote stopwatch tool handlers to call stopwatch.h functions:
     ```c
     static cJSON *handle_start_stopwatch(cJSON *id)
     {
       stopwatch_mcp_start();
       xiaozhi_voice_switch_to_stopwatch();
       printf("[mcp] stopwatch start requested, switching to stopwatch page\n");
       // ... build response with "秒表已启动"
     }
     static cJSON *handle_stop_stopwatch(cJSON *id)  { stopwatch_mcp_pause(); /* ... */ }
     static cJSON *handle_reset_stopwatch(cJSON *id)  { stopwatch_mcp_reset(); /* ... */ }
     static cJSON *handle_get_stopwatch_time(cJSON *id) { stopwatch_mcp_get_elapsed_ms(); /* ... */ }
     ```
